      "title": "epan: Fix GCC ASAN builds by marking two function tails \"not_reached\".",
      "message": "epan: Fix GCC ASAN builds by marking two function tails \"not_reached\".\n\nGCC seems unhappy with a WS_NORETURN function containing a trailing va_end\nafter its call to another WS_NORETURN function.  Even though the va_end is\nunreachable, the compiler incorrectly diagnoses that the outer function might\nreturn despite being marked \"noreturn\".  Rather than risking compiler wrath\nby deleting the balancing va_end, adding \"ws_assert_not_reached()\" in the two\naffected locations seems to make GCC happy when building with ASAN without\nbreaking anything else in my testing here (GCC 12 and LLVM/clang 14 on Debian\n12, Apple clang 16 on macOS 14.7.8).\n",
      "author_name": "Darius Davis",
      "author_email": "darius-wireshark@free-range.com.au",
